WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.687
A language model has never read a word in its life. It measures shadows.

2
00:00:06.967 --> 00:00:14.537
Here is an arrow, and a light. What lands on the floor is all the machine will ever know about it.

3
00:00:14.817 --> 00:00:15.978
- That's just a shadow.

4
00:00:16.258 --> 00:00:20.205
That is a dot product. Same thing, fancier name.

5
00:00:20.485 --> 00:00:32.884
Now turn it. Same arrow, same length. Point it the same way as the other one and the shadow is long. Turn it sideways and there is no shadow at all.

6
00:00:33.165 --> 00:00:34.372
- And past sideways?

7
00:00:34.652 --> 00:00:46.633
Then the shadow falls behind it and the number goes negative. One number, for how much two arrows agree. That is all a dot product is.

8
00:00:46.914 --> 00:00:52.440
Now the machine. Inside it, every word is an arrow. King, queen, banana, all arrows.

9
00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:59.175
Lay king's shadow on queen and it is long. Lay it on banana and there is barely anything.

10
00:00:59.455 --> 00:01:01.359
- So it never looked up what king means.

11
00:01:01.639 --> 00:01:08.419
It cannot. There is no dictionary in there, just a few thousand directions and a light.

12
00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:19.010
And attention, the word in every headline, is the same trick. One word throws its shadow onto every other word in the sentence at once.

13
00:01:19.289 --> 00:01:25.048
The long shadows are the words it listens to, and the slivers it ignores.

14
00:01:25.328 --> 00:01:27.139
- That's it? That's the whole trick?

15
00:01:27.419 --> 00:01:33.131
Billions of them a second, but yes. It is one shadow, done to death.

16
00:01:33.411 --> 00:01:43.442
It has never read a word. It measures how much two arrows agree, and it turns out that is enough. Comment SHADOW and I'll send you the card.
